Men and women need not be the same, any more than tourists and priests are
the same.  Ever since the different characters colored nethack, I have
greatly enjoyed the variety.  After all, it is a fantasy.  I'm out to be
somebody else for a while.

I think the tourist character is the perfect example how humor, stereotypes,
and bizarre logic can all convalesce deliciously into the fantasy.  And please
don't accuse me of being sexist.  Is it unfair to give more money to doctors,
more strength to barbarians, etc?  Dogs act like dogs, rust monsters act like
rust monsters...I think a greater gender distinction would be in the spirit
of the game, and lots of fun.

Tellya what though, I just brainstormed for five minutes and couldn't
think of any plausible extensions to the game involving gender distinction.

Perhaps someone else will?

